Z||000009||HYPTNOTiSE||09-26-2000||12:03 AM||||Ok, I'm going to get assinated for saying this, but I hate 3 things.<P>(1)- Tall wing stations for spoilers, When ever i see them, I just want to Karate Chop the spoiler.<P>(2) Holley scoups, Come on guys, really what are these doing for your car? Especially for 100-150 bucks!<P>(3) Cheezy 80's grahpics that say fiero really big, or have a big pegasus on the hood. It's like they're trying to combine the late 70's with the late 80's, Smokey and the bandit ring a bell? Well that was a firebird not a pegasus. Pegausi were not meant to be displayed on the hood of a fiero.<P>As far as the uglyiest fiero, it had to be the one that me and jeff were towing that cuaght fire, man that was ugly.<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||StuGood||09-26-2000||12:21 AM||||When I looked at that "Gator" hood, I laughed so hard I almost fell out of my chair!  Now, just put one of <B>those</B> on that ugly yellow and black "Fiero mini pickup (puke-up?) truck," and you'd have something.  What, I don't know, but don't park it in <B>my</B> driveway.   ||||reg||10
Z||000011||kevin||09-26-2000||01:58 AM||||That gator-job is heinous looking.There is no telling what depths the anti artistic among us will go.Before they market such a product, I think they should go to a local junior college art student to get their input before wasting time puting such idiocy on the road. The only benefit in those cars is to make the stock Fieros that much more beautiful.  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||rogergarrison||09-26-2000||05:52 AM||||Amen to the Gator hood, cant believe anyone buys them. Rear wings-well they dont do a d__n thing unless you drive over 150 mph. The absolutely dumbest thing I ever see (on any car) are these stupid wheels that stick out a foot past the side of car, I go into spasms laughing so hard when i see them. not to mention there eating wheel bearings like M&Ms. Also some of the paint jobs, colors, make me wonder what on earth owner is thinking. BTW, I think the faux yellow pickup is kinda cool, even though I dont like pickups either. All my opinions, everyone is entitled.||||reg||1
Z||000013||mrfixit58||09-26-2000||11:00 AM||||I didn't save the link but several months ago someone posted a picture of an interior that was recovered with yellow and white marine vinyl. It hut my eyes!<P>As far as the gray primer Fiero with the little fins on the front... he is in my Fiero club. A really nice guy. His interior is modified about as mush as his exterior. The car started life as a formula. I think it'll look pretty good if he ever gets around to painting it.<P>On a side note, he just got the car back from being stolen. He found it in a pond where it was submerged for eight days. he drained all the fluids and refilled the crank case and cylindars with oil, let the computer dry out, refilld all the fluids to the proper level and a week later fired it up. In less than a month he was driving it again. Gotta love his perseverance!<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||13
