Z||000039||BellaFiero||09-27-2000||10:20 AM||||You know... the Ricers, the Custom Guys, the Purists... they all have good points and bad. I personally like custom cars, heavily modded so it's almost not recognizable to stock. Our cars were abandoned by Pontiac - so I make it MY car the way I WANT it. Everything functional? Of course not. Not at highway speeds. Maybe if I strap an f-16 to her, then just maybe. The spoiler... uh, guys... the tall spoilers are just as effective as the factory spoilers - appearance only  (doubt me? go pour water on your stock spoiler and do 60 on the freeway ). The purple Fiero? ROCKS. That's alot of hard work put into that one, and I bet it scares the hell out of Ricers. The yellow Fiero? Not my style, but definitely someones. So I give him mad props. The Fi-Air-O over the roof scoops? Love em to death. Never trade them. They make my car look a little beefier, and the intimidation factor alone is awesome. Customizing cars is about a lot of things. But for me, it’s about creating a ride that thrills me. In drive, in style, in appearance. I would never drive a Sentra. Might be a nice car, but it just aint ME! And stock Fieros? Well… they’re sorta me. But I prefer my Fi-Air-O scoops, my tinted windows, my booming bass, my Kameleon CD player over the stock radio, the 6x9s under the dash, my polished aluminum black cherry –automatic- shifter ( with shift button cleverly disguised in the top ! Woohoo! Good for ten HP gain! ), black cherrry / wine paint job, my neon interior kit, my underbody neon kit, the Cobra Mini Jet hood scoop up front, my Custom sail panels with a blood-red Pegasus proudly proclaiming it’s Jayse’s Bella Donna, my Trans Am Ram Air racing stripes that vorpal the hood, and my… <P>… you get the idea. And you all can sit here and point and laugh and go “ha ha, that’s the stupidest looking thing.” But every where I go, I’ve got a legion of kids telling me how cool my car is, an army of custom body shops telling me I did good work for a 19 year old in his old man’s garage, and a plethora of girls who want me to take them for rides. <BR>So I aint got no worries.<BR>- - - - - - - - -<BR>You can have my semi-functional hood scoop when you pry it from my dead hands.<P><p>[This message has been edited by BellaFiero (edited 09-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000040||Phil||09-27-2000||10:21 AM||||The ugliest Fiero is anyone with me in it.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/New-sig.jpg"> <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000041||BellaFiero||09-27-2000||10:37 AM||||Incidentally, I say Bad Form to you Hypnotise. Maybe I'm reading this wrong, or maybe it's an inside joke, but those cars? I think those BELONG to Fiero5... I think those are his pride, his collection, and I think your last post just completely dissed them. Seriously... Bad Form. Even if they aren't Fiero5's cars, they belong to someone... <BR>...this next comment isn't directed at Hypnotise, so don't flame me man, but this is bad business right here, boys and girls. It's going to get alot of feelings hurt, and alot of pride will get tarnished. Flames will fly. Your talking about different cultures, different styles, regional attitudes, ethnic backgrounds... this could get ugly very fast. <BR>||||reg||1
