Z||000046||BellaFiero||09-27-2000||02:31 PM||||I will! Soon! I swear! Over the last weekend, it's been raining every day! Grrr and stuff! I swear, I go to grab the camera, and a rain cloud comes up. but here in Illinois, we're supposed to be having good weather for the next few days, so I'll be sure to get pics. Good ol' Wolf Camera will put them on CD for me, and I'll post them up here ASAP. I was a little hesitant at first, alot of the purists and what not WILL scoff at my car, but... then I figured, it's MY car... I didn't BUILD IT for anyone but ME.<P>And that concludes today's lesson  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000047||80's BOY||09-27-2000||03:17 PM||||i'll admit i had my feelings hurt after seeing the pictures of the Mercury cruiser. my interior looks EXACTLY like that without the cheesy console and gages. the outside was kinda ugly, and it DID resemble a boat in many ways, but it has a V8 and i don't so props to the guy that did it. as for me posting pics of my custom targa top and interior, honestly i'm scared to death to put them on here now!!!! i have a white car with slanted yellow lines and the rear of the car checkered black and white wrapping around to the rear deck lid from the doors back. custom targa, white and yellow seats with a grant black/yellow wheel. i just bought that cool security kit where you take the wheel off and lock the center cap on the column. i was so excited to share all these pics with you guys and now i'm hesitant to do so. just remember that everyone's got their own bag, and people shouldn't be scolded just because they do something to their cars that they like. let's all remember that there is a fine line between subtle mods and god-awful ugly mods that alot of people do not follow. some of those cars were really overdone in my opinion.||||reg||4
Z||000048||mrfixit58||09-27-2000||03:25 PM||||80's Boy,<P>Who care what people think... post em'. I've got a bone stock 87 GT that's factory Bubble Gum blue. Some people think that Fieros should only be Balck or Red. Who cares? I like blue. We may not prefer your color combination but different strokes for different folks! I would like to see your targa top.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000049||HugGRRRFiero||09-27-2000||04:00 PM||||80's boy,<P>I hope I didn't offend you.  I was just saying that the car mrfixit was talking about had a Mercruiser engine in it (actually it's a unique and neat idea, and the thought of making it into an amphibious vehicle would be "cool" and very unique too).   <P>Whether you post pictures of your car or not, you shouldn't be ashamed to post them.  It's your car, make it yours, it's what customizing is all about.  If I was worried about what others think of my Fiero, it would have been just another plain ol'black and 84 2M4 SE.  I hope I didn't offend anyone with a plain ol'black and 84 2M4 SE.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>&lt;zips up fire suit just in case&gt;<P>This thread is starting to unravel in a hurry.  I hope it doesn't start World War Thread Three!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  It's all fun and games until someone's car gets poked fun at.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000050||Fiero5||09-27-2000||04:09 PM||||I saw a Countach replica once that was for sale and it had been used in a few movies too. It was able to drive right into the water, as it had been designed to be air tight and float. It must have had a boat motor or some way to move once it's wheels lost contact. I will try and find the pic and post it. That was my favorite Kit car if I was to get one. Imagine going to the beach, and then just driving it right into the water and cruising around with the boats!!<BR>Steve||||reg||1
Z||000051||HugGRRRFiero||09-27-2000||04:37 PM||||Now that you say that, I remember a Countach that was in one of those "Cannon Ball Run" movies.  I remember there was one scene (bridge was out or something) and it skipped across the water and to the other side of the small river!  I wonder if that's the same car!||||reg||3
Z||000052||DaRkLoRD||09-27-2000||05:17 PM||||I'm planning to keep my GT appearing fairly stock.. on the outside at least.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>(I want to scrap the entire interior... I hate the fiero dash and gauges.. heheh)<P>as for the exterior, however, I would like 17" wheels.. a 1" drop.. tinted windows.. IRM sidescoops.. tom's decklid scoop.. custom hood scoops (based on corvette stingray side vents) low profile popup headlights, front airdam, driving lights, brighter tail light bulbs.. and *possibly* a VERY small and unobtrusive windshield banner.....<P>I think that's it.. I'm hoping it will look cool yet conservative enough that no one will think it's ugly.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000053||KitKar||09-27-2000||06:09 PM||||Personally I don't like stock fiero's. Or much anything else stock for that matter. So no matter how ugly a mod is, I think it is cool that somebody did it. At least they wanted to do something different.<BR>Same thing with the ricers. I question their choice of cars to modify, but at least they are doing something to improve their cars. Be it appearance or performance. So what if those combat wings aren't functional. They are different and look cool.<BR>Oh yeah, Fiero5's cars look cool too. Too stock for me, but at least he did something to improve them.<BR>Ok, I will step off my soap box now.<P>------------------<BR>Rick Lord<BR>Webmaster<BR>http://www.KitKar.com||||reg||1
Z||000054||DaRkLoRD||09-27-2000||06:49 PM||||oops..<p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 09-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000055||DaRkLoRD||09-27-2000||06:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KitKar:<BR><B>but at least they are doing something to improve their cars. Be it appearance or performance.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't think this counts as an improvement...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ricerocket.gif"> <P>in fact most true Ricer mods don't improve performance, OR appearance..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000056||Seanh||09-27-2000||07:54 PM||||When I was in Ogden UT last year. Parked in the Wal-Mart parking lot was a Blue 8?GT. He had done a bad job masking it off and painted it with what looked like common spray paint. The ground effects on it were painted yellow. From a distance it looked really good, but up close you could see his mistakes. It would look really cool IMO if he either did a better job painting it, or had it professionally painted. He had those Pep-boys leater seat overs on it and a woodgrain dash. I actually really like the car overall. The only fault was the bad masking job. Blue with Yellow ground effects looks great IMO.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000057||My7Fieros||09-27-2000||08:09 PM||||Lighten up people, dont start any flame wars. Be concious of criticizing forum members cars as well. This was simply meant as a light hearted discussion. Dont let it get out of hand, and if someone does bad mouth your car, blow it off. Everyone has the right to their own opinion.<P><BR>---------------<BR>"Always remember there are three kinds of people in the world.....those who can count, and those who cant."<BR><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 09-27-2000).]||||reg||8
