Z||000059||Fiero5||09-27-2000||10:11 PM||||"How can you say stickers improve a car?"<P>Isn't the style/look of the car one of the things that makes it special? What makes sports cars turn heads at first? The first impression is the look. No, the graphics don't give me hore HP or help me go faster, but when you are cruising down main street, it's not the extra horse power that turns the heads at 35 miles an hour, it's the LOOK!<BR>Just my thoughts :o)<BR>Steve<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000060||Seanh||09-27-2000||10:24 PM||||That movie your talking about it called "Speed Zone" and I am pretty sure that is the fiero your talking about. I probally shouldnt have posted about that car I saw in UT under this topic because by no means did I try to hint that is and ugly car. I know there is someone on this Forum from Ogden UT, might even be his car. I really love the color choice, but the masking job has room for improvment and I do know how dificult masking correctly is.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000061||StuGood||09-28-2000||08:09 PM||||Saddest-looking Fiero I ever saw was at a gas station here in Wichita, several years ago.  I was driving by, and the owner(?) was filling it up.  It might have been a 1988, because it was yellow.<P>...and the thing was melted down.  Engine fire, I assumed.  Poor thing looked like a dripping cheeseburger.<P>BTW, I apologize for my earier remark about the Fiero pickup.  I'm probably just jealous, because whoever owns that one can drive to the lumber yard in a Fiero, but I can't!<BR>  ||||reg||9
Z||000062||BBBAD GT||09-28-2000||08:38 PM||||I'll give you guys a little info on the Mercruiser Fiero, because I just met the guy a couple weeks ago.  <P>He does work for the boat industry (big around here in southern Illinois), and its obvious what his intent was.  That Mercruiser motor is straight out of a boat, and runs great.  He did something I've never seen, and thats running a 4cyl waterpump basically where the AC compressor was, and not haveing to cut anything.  That takes some time and effort to do, and I give him the highest kuddos for having the patients for it.  He's a really nice guy also, and I hope to go to other shows with him.<P>I know not everyone on here is intentionally putting down other owners Fieros, but please maybe think before you post.  Its the old "treat people how you want people to treat you" saying that I'm thinking of.  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000063||Fiero5||09-28-2000||08:40 PM||||One reason I add graphics to some of them, is that when you see a bunch of "plain" Fieros together, none of them really stand out. I still love the look of an "original" Fiero, which is why only a few of mine are done up like they are.<BR>I am sure that is why many customize their Fiero and add mods. It is to make it unique, their own and to make it stand out above the crowd and really get noticed! <BR> I drive my plain Fieros around alot too, but  I don't get a fraction of the response I get when driving one like my Fiero5 for example.<P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/files/My87Merrimack.jpg"> ||||reg||1
